 "readingTheResult": "The synthetic population is fitted per block group and placed at random within it (plus a pull toward care facilities), so need has no neighbor-scale pattern beyond what the block-group prior already holds. Smoothing can't beat the prior here by construction; this test can show whether it does harm, not whether it helps on real streets, where neighbors share building age, income and household type. Calibration below 1 means the homes that don't answer need help more often than the prior says: not answering is itself evidence of need.",
